# POKE - Change bytes in memory

```text
POKE address byte [byte ...]
```

Load a disposable program image with [GET](GET.HLP) before editing its
bytes. Addresses and values are hexadecimal. This writes 00 and C9 at
0100H and 0101H and reads them back:

```text
POKE 0100 00 C9
PEEK 0100 0101
```

The edit changes memory immediately. Use [SAVE](SAVE.HLP) with a new
filename to keep the edited image.
